1dc9-4127-811e-c15ccf85742d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788313775846218001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nCurrent-base archaeology shows that `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py:414-418` registers `review-code`, `review-plan`, and `sign-review`, but no bare `review` command. `docs/exit-codes.md:184`, `AGENTS.md:239-240`, and `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md:3` each still present bare `review` as an available forwarding shim or retained alias. Those operational guidance pages misstate the current CLI contract.\n\nHistorical records also mention the removed command: `docs/adr/0005-snapshot-cache-architecture.md:170` records a prior CLI/MCP mapping; `docs/release-notes.md:441` and `docs/output-schemas.md:263` expressly describe the surface as removed. Those records are not live guidance and must remain historical evidence rather than being rewritten.\n\n## Approach\n\nDelete the stale bare-`review` entry from `docs/exit-codes.md`. Rewrite the stale AGENTS LLM-operations guidance and `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md` CLI-form list to describe only live commands: `review-plan`, `review-code`, `sign-review` where applicable, `verify-completion`, and `scan-spec`. Do not alter the ADR or removal-history records. Retain accurate live-command exit-code rows unchanged except for immediately necessary table formatting. Do not add a command-reference generator and do not change the CLI registry: source inspection is the verification boundary, not an implementation target.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `docs/exit-codes.md` — remove the stale deprecated `review` shim row.\n- `AGENTS.md` — remove or rewrite the stale claim that bare `review` forwards to `review-plan`.\n- `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md` — remove bare `review` from its CLI forms and delete the retained-alias claim.\n- Read-only historical records: `docs/adr/0005-snapshot-cache-architecture.md`, `docs/release-notes.md`, and `docs/output-schemas.md` retain accurate past/removal references.\n- Read-only verification: `src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py` establishes the live command set.\n\n## Testing\n\nRun the existing documentation checks. Confirm the registry has no bare `review` route. Run `rg -n 'rebar review($|[^-])' AGENTS.md README.md docs`, then classify every residual hit: the only allowed historical hits are the ADR mapping row and the release-notes/output-schemas removed-surface records; any operational-guidance hit is a failure. Search the three edited operational pages for deprecated-forwarding and retained-alias wording.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] `docs/exit-codes.md` contains no row or prose that presents bare `review` as an available or forwarding CLI command.\n- [ ] `AGENTS.md` contains no claim that bare `review` forwards to `review-plan`.\n- [ ] `docs/repo-snapshot-gates.md` does not list bare `review` as a CLI form or retained alias.\n- [ ] The documented `review-code`, `review-plan`, and `sign-review` exit-code rows remain accurate and present.\n- [ ] The anchored guidance search has no operational-guidance `rebar review` hit; only the explicitly enumerated ADR/removal-history records may remain.\n- [ ] Existing documentation checks pass without expanding command-reference generation ownership.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"AGENTS.md","reason":"correct canonical agent guidance"},{"path":"docs/exit-codes.md","reason":"correct maintained exit-code guidance"},{"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_registry.py","reason":"verify source command ownership while updating docs"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyr